<Guide slug="stop-cash-going-missing" waMessage={WA_MESSAGES.guideCash} ctaTitle="See whose drawer was short, by name, tonight.">
  <p>
    Ask any owner of a shop, a bar, a restaurant or a petrol station and they will tell you the same story. The day was
    busy, the sales felt good, and the money in the drawer at night was less than it should have been. Not by a lot.
    A few hundred shillings. Then again the next week. Nobody can say where it went.
  </p>
  <p>
    Missing money is rarely one big theft. It is usually small amounts, often, in places nobody is looking: a sale
    that was never rung up, a void after the customer left, change counted wrong in a rush, a "friend's" drink, stock
    that walked out of the store. Some of it is honest mistakes. Some of it is not. Either way, you cannot fix what you
    cannot see.
  </p>
  <p>This guide is about making it visible, by name and by day, without accusing anyone.</p>

  <h2>1. One drawer, one person, every shift</h2>
  <p>
    If three people work from one cash drawer, a shortage belongs to nobody. Give each cashier their own drawer, or at
    least their own shift on it, and a count when they start and when they hand over. It feels slower for a week.
    After that it is simply how the counter works.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Count the float in.</strong> The opening cash is counted and written down before the first sale, by the person who will be responsible for it.</li>
    <li><strong>Count it out.</strong> At the end of the shift, the cash is counted before anyone else touches the drawer.</li>
    <li><strong>Sign it off.</strong> Over or short, the number is agreed on the spot, not argued about next morning.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="guide-zt">
    <p class="guide-zt__h">How ZapTill does it</p>
    <p>
      Each cashier signs in to the point of sale with their own PIN and counts their float when the shift opens. At the
      day close, every drawer is counted and ZapTill shows the cash expected, the cash counted and the M-Pesa total for
      each cashier, with who was over and who was short.
    </p>
  </div>

  <figure>
    <Monitor label="The real ZapTill point of sale asking the cashier to count the float">
      <Shot src="/screens/till-float.webp" width={1280} height={800}
        alt="The real ZapTill point of sale: 'Open your drawer. Wanjiru, count the cash in it', with a box for the opening float. A demo business." />
    </Monitor>
